window.KB_BODY[60]={"tsb101669":"<h2>Piston Protrusion</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is being issued to correct the specifications for Piston Protrusion for Emission Controlled Engines published in Procedure 001-054 of the troubleshooting and repair manual.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101676":"<h2>Revision to Crankcase Blowby, Measure Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates common Procedure 014-010 Crankcase Blowby, Measure. Updates were made to the Crankcase Blowby, Measure chart in the General Information that will be used on all Midrange diesel engines.</p><p>Blowby specifications have been added for new engines, rebuilt engines, and for troubleshooting.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101677":"<h2>New Straight Thread Plug</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new straight thread plug that will be used on all MidRange engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and not subject to campaign.</p></div></div><p>The new straight thread plug (2) has a pre-applied sealant. The previous straight thread plug (1) had a removable/replaceable o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/17900065.png\" alt=\"17900065.png\"></figure><p>The two plugs are interchangeable and reusable. The <b>only</b> difference between them is the installation torque value.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Straight Thread Plug with O-Ring</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Size</td><td>Part Number*</td><td>O-ring Part Number</td><td>Torque</td></tr><tr><td>M10</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678923\">3678923</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678925\">3678925</a></td><td>10 N•m [89 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M12</td><td>3678910</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678603\">3678603</a></td><td>20 N•m [177 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M14</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678921\">3678921</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678912\">3678912</a></td><td>25 N•m [221 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M16</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089567\">3089567</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3679139\">3679139</a></td><td>35 N•m [25 ft-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M18</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678873\">3678873</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678786\">3678786</a></td><td>45 N•m [33 ft-lb]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>* Part number includes o-ring.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Straight Thread Plug with Formed Pre-Applied Sealant</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Size</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Torque</td></tr><tr><td>M10</td><td>3977851</td><td>18 N•m [160 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M12</td><td>3977852</td><td>25 N•m [221 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M14</td><td>3977853</td><td>30 N•m [22 ft-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M16</td><td>3977854</td><td>40 N•m [30 ft-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>M18</td><td>3977855</td><td>50 N•m [37 ft-lb]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Both styles of plugs, and o-rings for straight thread plugs with o-rings, are available for service. Either plug can be used when a replacement plug is needed. The correct installation torque <b>must</b> be used.</p><p>The straight thread plug with pre-applied sealant can be reinstalled until the pre-applied sealant becomes damaged. Once damaged, the plug <b>must</b> be replaced. New sealant can <b>not</b> be applied.</p><p>Procedure 017-011, Straight Thread Plug, has been updated to include this new service information.</p>","tsb101692":"<h2>Revision to Service Tools Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information on the revision of Procedure 022-001, Service Tools for the 6C and C8.3 series engines. A new service tool has been released to remove the fuel pump gear.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101698":"<h2>Change in Engine Brake Running Clearance Minimum Specifications</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic introduces a change in the minimum specification of the engine brake rocker lever running clearance for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 engines. The change has been made to add a safety margin to accommodate exhaust valve stem growth.</p><p>The table below contains the new and the previous running clearance limits.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Previous Specification</td><td>0.508</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.020</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>2.79</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.110</td></tr><tr><td>New Specification</td><td>0.635</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.025</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>2.79</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.110</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb101723":"<h2>Revision to Procedure 016-002, Engine Support Bracket, Front</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 016-002 in the Signature, ISX and QSX15 Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>The torque procedure and specifications for the front engine support bracket capscrews are being updated to the same procedure and specifications as used at initial engine assembly.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Old Torque Specification</th><th>New Torque Specification</th><th>Engines Affected</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>165 N•m [122 ft-lb]</td><td>97 N•m + 60 degrees [72 ft-lb + 60 degrees]</td><td>Signature, ISX, QSX15</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101752":"<h2>Revision to Procedure 020-012, Engine Brake Solenoid Valve</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a change in the troubleshooting and repair Procedure 020-112, Engine Brake Solenoid Valve for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The changes made are in the Inspect for Reuse section, to resistance check values for a 12-volt supply solenoid and to the measurement method.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><p>Resistance Values</p><p>The cold engine and hot engine resistance values should be between 5 and 20 ohms for solenoids that require a supply of 12 volts.</p><p>The table below indicates the old and new resistance check values for a 12-volt supply:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine State</th><th>Old Resistance Value</th><th>New Resistance Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cold</td><td>8 to 10 ohms</td><td>5 to 20 ohms</td></tr><tr><td>Hot</td><td>16 to 20 ohms</td><td>5 to 20 ohms</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Measurement Method</p><p>In order to eliminate any measurement error, follow the steps below to check the resistance of the solenoid:</p><ul><li>Disconnect the wiring harness.</li><li>Measure the resistance from the terminal to the body of the solenoid, as indicated in the illustration.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/20c00099.png\" alt=\"20c00099.png\"></figure>","tsb101755":"<h2>Revision to Crankshaft Gear, Adapter, and Tone Wheel Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes Topic 07T1-1; replace 07T1-1 with this topic.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information for the removal and installation of the Crankshaft Adapter (Procedure 001-017), Crankshaft Gear (Procedure 001-018), and the Crankshaft Tone Wheel (Procedure 001-069). These procedures were developed to avoid the unnecessary replacement of the crankshaft in the field due to a crankshaft adapter, crankshaft gear or tone wheel repair.</p>","tsb101756":"<h2>Revision to Engine Vibration Excessive Troubleshooting Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the Engine Vibration Excessive <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>-t075 troubleshooting symptom tree for the ISX and QSX engine family. This topic adds a step to check the Vibration Damper, which was omitted from the previous tree.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101759":"<h2>Revised Fan Idler Assembly</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This Service/Parts Topic 06T3-8A supersedes 06T3-8: replace 06T3-8 with this one.</p></div></div><p>The purpose of this revised Service/Parts Topic is to announce that topic 06T3-8A incorporates the reference to the Service Manual, Bulletin Reference <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>, which supersedes the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin Reference 3666261. Also to correct an error that was present on the version published on Quick Serve On Line.</p><p>This service topic details the procedures for removal/installation of the revised fan idler arrangement for the QSK45, QSK60 series engines.</p><p>The revised fan idler, slide arm type, went into production in August 2004 at the Daventry Engine plant. Engine serial number first was 33157417.</p><p>This service topic details the procedures for removal/installation of the revised fan idler arrangement for the QSK45 and QSK60 series engines.</p>","tsb101763":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Filter, Improved Venturi Oil Filter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a modification to the Heavy Duty line of Fleetguard™ lubricating oil filters.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Lubricating Oil Filter Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fleetguard™</td><td>LF9000</td><td>LF9001</td><td>LF9031</td></tr><tr><td>Cummins</td><td>3101868</td><td>3101869</td><td>4906633</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Since these filters are being released as a product improvement, there will be no change in part numbers because the form, fit, and function remain unchanged.</p></div></div><p>The venturi design has been optimized to better distribute oil flow during normal engine operation; however during extreme engine oil conditions (additive dropout, contamination, soot etc.) the improvements increase the overall filtration effectiveness.</p><p>While the oil flow control device enhances filtration, it is imperative that the recommended oil and filter change guidelines be followed. Refer to the Operation and Maintenance Manuals, Bulletin 4021345 for ISX.</p><p>These filters are being released for all present production heavy duty applications which use an engine mounted oil filter. These revised lubricating oil filters can also be used on any application which is presently capable of using the LF9000, LF9001, and LF9031 filters.</p><p>The date code on the bottom of the filter can be used to identify whether the oil flow control device has been added to the venturi.</p><p>Engines built prior to October 7, 2005, were produced with a lubricating oil filter that did not utilize the added improvements, including the modified flow control device in the venturi.</p><p>Engines built after October 7, 2005, were produced with a lubricating oil filter with a date code 05258 or higher, which feature the new oil flow venturi with the added oil flow control device. The engine serial number first (ESN) for ISX engines is 79136878.</p><p>For proper lubricating oil filter installation, refer to Procedure 007-013 in the Signature, ISX and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101773":"<h2>Revision to Engine Brake Piston Procedure, Actuator Piston Reuse</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a revision in the Remove and Inspect for Reuse steps in Procedure 020-019, Engine Brake Piston. The change made is in the event of an actuator piston malfunction on a lever. Replace the lever that contains the malfunctioning actuator piston.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101774":"<h2>Symptom Tree, Coolant Loss - Internal</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises troubleshooting symptom tree <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>-t021, Coolant Loss - Internal. The revisions direct the user to pressure test the cooling system prior to removing the cylinder head and, if no visible coolant leaks or rapid pressure loss is observed, to replace the injector o-rings and install the injectors to specification.</p><p>Confirm there are no coolant leaks on any of the components listed in the list below and pressure test the cooling system as described in Procedure 008-018 in the Signature, ISX and QSX15 Service Manual. If no rapid pressure loss is observed and no visual indications of bubbles or wetness exist in the exhaust ports, replace the injector o-rings and install the injectors as described in Procedure 006-026 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual. If pressure loss or visual indications of bubbles are observed, inspect the head for cracks or porosity as described in Procedure 002-004 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual. If no bubbles are observed and no visual indication of cracks are present, replace the injector o-rings and install the injectors.</p><p>Check the following component locations for external coolant loss:</p><ol><li>Air compressor cylinder head</li><li>EGR cooler</li><li>Lubricating oil cooler</li><li>Fuel heater</li><li>Transmission oil cooler or torque converter cooler</li><li>Cylinder head gasket leaking.</li></ol>","tsb101775":"<h2>Service Tools Page Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides updates to the service tools page for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual. The Crankshaft Adapter and Gear Remover Kit, Part Number 4918530, has been added, along with several other revisions to reflect the previous tool improvements.</p>","tsb101776":"<h2>Converted Schematic Cooling System Flow Diagrams</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic converts Cooling System flow diagrams for the QSK45 and QSK60 Series engines from schematic drawings to on-engine flow diagrams which illustrate the jacket water circuit, LTA water circuit, and vent line flow.</p>","tsb101779":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Filter, Improved Venturi Oil Filter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a modification to the Heavy Duty line of Fleetguard™ lubricating oil filters.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Lubricating Oil Filter Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fleetguard™</td><td>LF9000</td><td>LF9001</td><td>LF9031</td></tr><tr><td>Cummins</td><td>3101868</td><td>3101869</td><td>4906633</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Since these filters are being released as a product improvement, there will be no change in part numbers because the form, fit, and function remain unchanged.</p></div></div><p>The venturi design has been optimized to better distribute oil flow during normal engine operation; however during extreme engine oil conditions (additive dropout, contamination, soot etc.) the improvements increase the overall filtration effectiveness.</p><p>While the oil flow control device enhances filtration, it is imperative that the recommended oil and filter change guidelines be followed. Refer to the Operation and Maintenance Manuals, Bulletin 4021342 for ISM.</p><p>These filters are being released for all present production heavy duty applications which use an engine mounted oil filter. These revised lubricating oil filters can also be used on any application which is presently capable of using the LF9000, LF9001, and LF9031 filters.</p><p>The date code on the bottom of the filter can be used to identify whether the oil flow control device has been added to the venturi.</p><p>Engines built prior to October 7, 2005, were produced with a lubricating oil filter that did not utilize the added improvements, including the modified flow control device in the venturi.</p><p>Engines built after October 7, 2005, were produced with a lubricating oil filter with a date code 05258 or higher, which features the new oil flow venturi with the added oil flow control device. The engine serial number first (ESN) for the ISM engine is 3514172.</p><p>For proper lubricating oil filter installation, refer to Procedure 007-013 in the ISM, ISM e, and QSM11 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/manual/3666322\">3666322</a>.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>this is a product improvement and is not subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101791":"<h2>Cylinder Head Reuse for Update from 13-Piece to Single-Piece Cylinder Head Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents specific criteria for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Cummins engines built before September, 2001, equipped with a 13-piece head gasket and grooved liners. Cylinder Head Procedure 002-004 and Cylinder Head Gasket Procedure 002-021 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>, are being revised to include this information. Recent testing has determined that upgrading to a one-piece head gasket and flattop liners is more resistant to combustion leaks than the 13-piece head gasket and grooved liners. The repair is especially applicable for customers who have had head gasket failures on engines which are <b>not</b> ready or scheduled for overhaul.</p><p>This information addresses coolant leaks, caused by combustion gases being pushed into the coolant passages or during repairs in which out-of-specification liner recession is measured. Cummins Distributors and Dealers are encouraged to use their technical expertise to implement these guidelines for low cost, high quality repair of Cummins products.</p><p>This change in the &#x27;Reuse Guidelines&#x27; does <b>not</b> apply to instances when, after the cylinder head has been cleaned, there is detectable depth across the sealing area between two cylinders or between a cylinder coolant passage and a capscrew hole.</p><p>This change to the reuse guidelines <b>only</b> applies to the ESN range before 14022616. Based on the results of Service Engineering analysis and endurance testing, upgrading to a one-piece head gasket and flattop liners reduces susceptibility to coolant leaks. Wear in the area where the fire ring combustion seal contacts the cylinder head is now acceptable when replacing a 13-piece cylinder head gasket and grooved liners with a one-piece cylinder head gasket and flattop liners. To prevent possible damage to the cylinder head during the repair, proper cleaning procedures and all other reuse guidelines <b>must</b> be checked and followed as stated in the Cylinder Head Procedure 002-004, in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><p>This information applies specifically to ESN 14022616 and earlier, and addresses reuse due to erosion in the sealing area around the combustion surface. For engines outside of this ESN range, Cummins Distributors and Dealers are encouraged to continue to follow the &#x27;Inspect for Reuse&#x27; steps in Cylinder Head Procedure 002-004 in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a></p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Cylinder Head Gasket Part Number Information</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td><td>Old Part Number (13-Piece Gasket with Grooved Liners)</td><td>New Part Number (One-Piece Gasket with Flattop Liners)</td></tr><tr><td>Gasket Set</td><td>1</td><td>4025287</td><td>4025300</td></tr><tr><td>Liner Kit</td><td>6</td><td>3800453</td><td>4089153</td></tr><tr><td>Ring Set</td><td>6</td><td>4089154</td><td>4089154</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00145.png\" alt=\"02c00145.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00146.png\" alt=\"02c00146.png\"></figure><p>Service Tool Part number 3165071</p><p>Service Tool Part number 3164442</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear in the area that the fire ring combustion seal contacts the head is now acceptable when replacing a 13-piece head gasket and grooved liners with a one-piece head gasket and flattop liners.</p></div></div><p>This change in Reuse Guidelines does <b>not</b> apply to instances when, after the cylinder head has been cleaned, there is detectable depth across the sealing area between two cylinders or between a cylinder and coolant passage or a cylinder and capscrew hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00147.png\" alt=\"02c00147.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00066.png\" alt=\"02c00066.png\"></figure><p>Depth Across Sealing Area</p><p>Leak Path Between Cylinder and Cylinder Head Capscrew Hole</p><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Failure to insert the oil passage plugs can result in a connecting rod bearing failure, main bearing failure, or both.</p></div></div><p>Immediately upon removal of the cylinder head, plugs <b>must</b> be installed into the oil passage drillings in both the cylinder head and the block. The plugs are necessary to prevent debris from entering the lubrication system during the repair.</p><p>Prior to cleaning the combustion face of the cylinder head, small rubber plugs, Part number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4089255\">4089255</a>, and tape <b>must</b> be used to plug or cover the oil supply holes at the ends of the cylinder head to prevent debris from entering the oil passages.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00111.png\" alt=\"02c00111.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02c00142.png\" alt=\"02c00142.png\"></figure><p>Clean Cylinder Head</p><p>Protective Plug Locations</p><p>Use Scotch-Brite™ 7448 abrasive hand pad, Part Number 3823258, or equivalent, to clean the cylinder head combustion face. Also make sure there is no loose debris sitting in the valve pockets around the head of the valve.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use power tools to clean the combustion face of the cylinder head.</p><p>For more information on the Protective Plug Kit, consult the Remove step in the Cylinder Head Procedure 002-004, in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb101792":"<h2>Revision to Crosshead Procedure, Crosshead Pocket Inspection</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic changes the inspection criteria in valve crossheads for QSK45/60 diesel engines. The change adds reuse criteria for the valve stem pocket in the crosshead. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-002-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-001 in Section 2</a> of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101795":"<h2>Engine Brake Control Procedure Revision, VGT Engine Braking</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises information in Procedure 213-007, Engine Brake Control, to include the use of the Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT) for engine braking on the ISB-CM850 engines, since conventional engine brakes are <b>not</b> an option.</p>","tsb101811":"<h2>Crankcase Vent Hose Modification for Cold Weather</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a modification to the crankcase vent hose on Signature, ISX, and QSX15 engines operating in cold weather. This modification can be made to any vehicles that may be operating in ambient temperatures from -23°C [-10°F] and below.</p><p>The following illustration shows the basic routing of the original crankcase vent hose.</p><p>The approximate length of the crankcase vent hose ranged from 168 cm [66 in] to 112 cm [44 in] in length.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07c00313.png\" alt=\"07c00313.png\"></figure><p>The illustration below shows the new routing for the crankcase vent hose.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07c00312.png\" alt=\"07c00312.png\"></figure>","tsb101822":"<h2>Two Pump, Two Loop Cooling System Diagram</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds an exploded view to Procedure 100-002, with the two pump, two loop cooling system configuration.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08a00192.png\" alt=\"08a00192.png\"></figure><p>Non-Thermostatically Controlled Two Pump Two Loop Cooling System</p><ol><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump inlet</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump support bracket</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer connection</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water outlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water outlet.</li></ol>","tsb101845":"<h2>Service Tool Page Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information on the Cylinder Head Fuel Passage Leak Test Kit, Part Number 3164943, for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 series engines.</p>","tsb101850":"<h2>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Introduction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes and replaces Service/Parts Topics 97t0-7 and 99t0-22.</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the introduction of the QST30 Tier 2, Tier 1, non-certified products, and identifies unique engine components for the non-certified products.</p><p>The QST30 Tier 2 engine is redesigned to address the US Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) exhaust emissions levels for off-highway engines in the &gt;560 kW [&gt;751 HP] power category built after 01 January 2006. It is built to meet and exceed present and future competitive pressures, worldwide emissions regulations, and corporate standards for performance, reliability and durability.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Industrial</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td><td>D573003CX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td><td>30.5 liters [1861 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>15.7:1</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled</td><td>Turbocharged and 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Power Generation</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573001GX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled, 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled, Jacket Water Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3112 kg [6860 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Ratings (Industrial)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine.</p><p>The Tier 2 ratings shown below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Configuration Number - D573002CX03</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option Number</td><td>CPL Number</td><td>Power kW [bhp] @ rpm</td><td>Peak Torque N•m [ft-lb] @ rpm</td><td>Rating Type</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5234</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 2100</td><td>5084 [3750] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5235</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 1900</td><td>5085 [3751] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5236</td><td>1244</td><td>820 [1100] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5237</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5239</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1900</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5238</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5240</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5241</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5242</td><td>1244</td><td>708 [950] @ 2100</td><td>4188 [3089] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5243</td><td>1244</td><td>671 [900] @ 2100</td><td>3747 [2764] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5244</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 2000</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5245</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 1800</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Continuous</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5246</td><td>1244</td><td>567 [760] @ 2100</td><td>3350 [2471] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Engine Ratings (Power Generation)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine. The QST30 Tier 2 ratings shown in the table below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings can be requested by submitting a Value Package Change Request (VPCR). Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th>Standby</th><th>Prime</th><th>Continuous</th><th>Cooling</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FR 5247</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>2P2L</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5250</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>ATA</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30 Industrial Tier 1 service parts topic introduced the Tier 1 emission-certified QST30 engine for mobile off-highway applications. A new procedure for the charge-air cooler (CAC), a new symptom tree, and revisions to five other symptom trees were also included in the Tier 1 engine introduction.</p><p>To meet year 2000 Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) and California Air Resources Board (CARB) Tier 1 emission levels, it was necessary to change the non-certified QST30 aspiration from turbocharged and jacket water aftercooled (JWAC) to turbocharged and charge-air cooled (CAC). The Tier 1 product employs two separate cooling circuits; A liquid-coolant-filled high-temperature circuit (HTC) for the main engine jacket water cooling, and a low-temperature, air-to-air circuit (LTC) for charge-air cooling. This topic addressed <b>only</b> the differences between the Tier 1 and non-certified QST30 Industrial engines.</p><p>Charge-air cooling of the intake air was required to retain engine efficiency while injection timing was retarded to obtain lower NOx. Charge-air cooling also allowed higher horsepower capabilities for the equivalent thermal loading. In addition to the non-certified QST30 power ranges of 760 hp to 1050 hp, a 1200 hp with 6000-foot altitude capability became available. The new offering also featured a 25 percent torque rise and is restricted to intermittent applications with load factors equal to or less than 40 percent.</p><p>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 limited production began 01 January 2000 and retained the configuration number D573002CX03.</p><p>For general charge-air cooling installation guidelines, see the Application Engineering Bulletin Number 3884966, (AEB) 24.06 - 1999 Industrial Application Installation Recommendations, Charge-Air Cooling.</p><p>Emission Regulations</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Year 2000 Tier 1 Emission Regulations</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Emission Regulating Agency</td><td>Emission Limit (g/bhp-hr) NOx</td><td>Horsepower</td></tr><tr><td>CARB</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr><tr><td>EPA</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ratings</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The <b>only</b> difference between CPL 2640 and CPL 2818 is the orientation of the turbocharger compressor housings. The base turbocharger part number is the same for the two CPLs.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 Ratings</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine Model</td><td>Rated Horsepower kW [bhp] rpm, N•m [ft-lb] rpm</td><td>Application</td><td>CPL</td><td>ECM Code</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>669 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4103 [3026]@1300 rpm</td><td>Komatsu WA900, front-out exhaust</td><td>2640</td><td>K50017</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>807 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4629 [3414]@1400 rpm</td><td>Komatsu 330M, rear-out exhaust, with PMC, with CENSE™</td><td>2818</td><td>K50019</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>567 [760]@2100 rpm. Torque peak: 3350 [2471]@1300 rpm</td><td>Kawasaki 135Z</td><td>2640</td><td>K50018</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial service parts topic announced the introduction of the QST30-C Industrial engine.</p><p>New industrial ratings of the QST30 engine were released for limited production in September, 1997. Four ratings of this industrial engine were released. The QST30-C uses many of the successfully proven technologies already in production on QST30 Power Generation engines. The QST30-C uses a full-authority electronic Bosch® fuel system, Cummins Inc. developed controls, and is fully compatible with the CENSE™ engine monitoring system. QST30-C Industrial ratings are designed to replace V28 and lower K38 ratings with improved fuel economy, transient response, emissions, and diagnostic capabilities.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30-C Non-Certified Industrial</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Model Name</td><td>QST30-1050</td></tr><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td></tr><tr><td>CPL</td><td>2127</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Code</td><td>105</td></tr><tr><td>Injector (Qty.)</td><td>3092022 (2), 3092023 (10)</td></tr><tr><td>Crankshaft</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092922\">3092922</a></td></tr><tr><td>Camshft (Qty.)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092971\">3092971</a> (1), <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092974\">3092974</a> (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Piston (Qty.)</td><td>3092606 (6), 3092607, (6).</td></tr><tr><td>Turbocharger (Qty.)</td><td>3537114 (1), 3097115 (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Cylinder Head</td><td>3094190</td></tr><tr><td>Horsepower</td><td>1050 hp @ 2100 rpm</td></tr><tr><td>Torque</td><td>3415 ft-lb @ 1300 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial engine contains several unique parts. A general description of these components and a listing of parts that are not shared with the power generation QST30 engines. Components are organized by group for ease of use.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QST30-C engines used in Komatsu applications will be Komatsu branded and designated SA12V140 Z-1. They will <b>not</b> be Cummins Inc. labeled or identified as QST30-C. The engines in Komatsu applications are <b>not</b> covered by Cummins Inc. warranty, and they will be serviced through the Komatsu service network.</p></div></div>","tsb101871":"<h2>Main Bearing Capscrew Torque Specification Change</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic supersedes 05T1-7. Please replace 05T1-7 with this topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts topic updates the torque procedure for ISX Main Bearing caps in Procedure 001-006.</p><p>The new torque value of 149 N•m [110 ft-lb] plus 180° has been validated for the MEX blocks (blocks after ESN 79012120) and will now be used on all engines.</p><p>The procedure change will affect <b>only</b> the torque specification. This eliminates the dual torque specifications on the ISX engine.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101872":"<h2>Revision to Procedure Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly, New Torque Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises, Procedure 001-054, Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly. The torque procedure has been revised</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101882":"<h2>Add Fault Code 72-fc731</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is adding fault code 72-fc731, Engine Speed Sensor and Camshaft Position Sensor - Mechanical Misalignment Between Camshaft and Crankshaft Sensors. The fault code addition is for the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 engines with CM570.</p>","tsb101885":"<h2>Engine Testing (Engine Dynamometer)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information on the revision of Procedures 014-005 and 014-006, Engine Testing (Engine Dynamometer) for the QSK45 and QSK60 series engines. This topic updates the procedure for the use of the engine control, the INLINE™5 datalink adapter kit, and the engine control harness installation on electronically actuated injector engines.</p>","tsb101886":"<h2>Update to Procedure 001-054 (Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly), Addition of Missing Procedure Steps</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to update procedure 001-054 with the missing Disassemble, Clean and Inspect for Reuse, Assemble, and Install steps.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This change will <b>not</b> release any new parts or affect any part numbers.</p></div></div>","tsb101890":"<h2>Fuel Drain Line Restriction, Pressure Gauge</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is revising Procedure 006-012, Fuel Drain Line Restriction. The update is changing the adapter part number and is replacing the manometer gauge with a pressure gauge.</p>","tsb101900":"<h2>Service Tools Page, Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information on the Engine Control, Part Number 3163890. The Engine Control, Part Number 3163890, is used with the Engine Control Harness Part Number 4918643, for engines with electronically actuated injectors or the Engine Control Harness Part Number 3163891, for engines with mechanically actuated injectors, to operate the engine out-of-chassis.</p>","tsb101910":"<h2>Valve Guide Seals, Cylinder Head</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic indicates a change in Procedure 002-016, Valve Guide Seal, Cylinder Head. The changes made in the procedure and as indicated below clarify the usage of the valve guide seals.</p><p>The present production engines use valve guide seal, Part Number 4026791, for both intake and exhaust valve guides, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4026657\">4026657</a>; these were introduced in March 2002. The present production valve guide seal, Part Number 4026791, can be used in place of intake valve guide seal, Part Number 4026660, and exhaust valve guide seal, Part Number 4026791, that were used in engine built from 15 May 2000 to the end of February 2002.</p><p>Engines built prior to Engine Serial Number (ESN) 14010274 should use intake valve guide seal, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4003966\">4003966</a>, and exhaust valve guide seal, Part Number 3606766 and can <b>not</b> use the present production valve guide seal, Part Number 4026791.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Compatibility Table</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>Engines Built Before ESN 14010274</td><td>Engines Built from 15 May 2000 to end of February 2002</td><td>Production Engines (After March 2002)</td></tr><tr><td>Valve Guide</td><td>3680867</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4026657\">4026657</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4026657\">4026657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Valve Guide Seals</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4003966\">4003966</a>, Intake</td><td>4026660, Intake</td><td>4026791, Intake and Exhaust</td></tr><tr><td>3606766, Exhaust</td><td>4026791, Exhaust</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Compatibility</td><td>Parts <b>not</b> compatible with engines built after ESN 14010274</td><td>Production valve guide seals are backwards compatible to ESN 14010274</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101914":"<h2>Revision to Procedure Overhead Set</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a Measure step to Procedure 003-004, Overhead Set.</p>","tsb101915":"<h2>Revision to Gear Lash Procedure Graphic</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic identifies the graphic change for adjusting back lash when setting base engine timing in the Adjust step of Procedure 001-088, Engine Base Timing. The fourth graphic in the step did show the same location of the shim for both the top and bottom of the idler gear. Gear lash is consistently set on the load side of the teeth. A graphic change has been made to show the load location on the top of the idler gear is opposite of the load location on the bottom of the idler gear.</p>","tsb101919":"<h2>Revision to Procedure Overhead Set</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 003-004 Overhead Set. A measurement step has been added to the procedure.</p>","tsb101926":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Update - Centinel™ Oil Replacement Interval</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance schedule for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines. The revision adds a new maintenance item under the interval of Maintenance Procedures at 250 Hours or 6 Months, and a new interval to the schedule for engines utilizing the Centinel™ oil system.</p>","tsb101929":"<h2>Symptom Tree Revision, Oil Pressure High</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree, <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>-t104, Lubricating Oil Pressure High, to update a procedure reference for correction, when the pressure regulator valve is stuck open.</p>","tsb101933":"<h2>Revision to Lower Idler Gear Remove and Install</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic identifies the process error for removing and installing the lower idler gear. The use of a guide stud is specified for removal and installation of the gear in Procedure 001-088 of the service manual. The gear needs to be lifted over the crankshaft tone wheel to be removed and installed. The use of a guide stud will <b>not</b> allow the gear to be removed or installed.</p>","tsb101934":"<h2>Flywheel Capscrew Socket Tool Part Number</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic identifies the need to add the flywheel mounting capscrew socket part number and correct a capscrew size in Procedure 016-005 of the service manual. The 21mm impact socket, Part Number 3162813, is <b>not</b> listed. The flywheel mounting capscrews and guide studs listed as M6 should be M16.</p>","tsb101939":"<h2>Fuel Lift Pump, Mounting Plate Torque Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic provides information on the mounting plate torque revision in Procedure 005-045, Fuel Lift Pump.</p>","tsb101940":"<h2>Air Compressor Procedures, Carbon Removal Information</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the following procedures to the ISM Service Manual and converts the procedures from engine specific to common procedures to be used for both the ISX and ISM series engines.</p><ul><li>Procedure 012-003, Air Compressor Carbon Buildup</li><li>Procedure 012-007, Air Compressor Cylinder Head, Single Cylinder</li><li>Procedure 012-024, Air Pressure Relief Valve.</li></ul>","tsb101957":"<h2>Revision to Fuel Inlet Restriction Procedure, Tool Name Change</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the service tool noun name from Diagnostic Orifice Tool, to Fuel System Tester, Part Number 4918612, to provide consistency between all sources of information.</p>","tsb101963":"<h2>Reference Amendment in Procedure 005-999</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to amend a reference in Procedure 005-999 in the C-Series Troubleshooting and Repair Manual. The change is the reference to Procedure 006-003 (Air in Fuel) for bleeding air from the fuel system, in place of Procedure 006-001 (AFC Air Tube).</p>","tsb101969":"<h2>Procedure for Head Casting Erosion Repair</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new service kit used to repair cylinder head erosion around the intake ports.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Each kit contains intake port plugs, epoxy filler material, releasing agent, a drill bit, and tool instructions. This kit can be used for multiple repairs, depending on the amount of filler material required.</p></div></div><p>The kit contains the following:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Cylinder Head Repair Kit, Part Number 4918684</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Description</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Quanity</td></tr><tr><td>Compound, Metal Repair</td><td>4918685</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Plug, Protective</td><td>4918686</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Drill</td><td>4918687</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Compound, Releasing</td><td>4918691</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Bulletin, Tool Instructions</td><td>3400222</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb101978":"<h2>Revision to Engine Diagrams Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds five views of the QSK60 single stage with electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb101986":"<h2>Revision to Cooling Fan Drive Belt</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a caution applying to the removal of the cooling fan belt for all C and L series engines equipped with an automatic belt tensioner. The caution warns against the use of a socket extension when removing and installing the cooling fan belt. The improper use of a socket extension can cause the automatic belt tensioner arm to break.</p>","tsb101990":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Update</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds &#x27;Turbocharger - Replace (QSK60 Modular Common Rail System Single Stage Turbocharged Haul Truck Application 2700HP Rating <b>ONLY</b>)&#x27; and &#x27;Turbocharger - Replace (QSK60 Modular Common Rail System Single Stage Turbocharged Haul Truck Application 2500HP Rating <b>ONLY</b>)&#x27; to the Maintenance Schedule.</p>","tsb101994":"<h2>Revision to Fault Code Accelerator Position Sensor Circuit, Step 2C</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Step 2C, directing the user to disconnect the accelerator position sensor before checking the resistance. The resistance between the supply wire and the signal wire should read over 100K ohms.</p>","tsb101995":"<h2>Fault Code Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is revising the following Fault Codes.</p><ul><li>Fault Code 153, Intake Manifold Air Temperature Sensor Circuit - Voltage Above Normal or Shorted to High Source.</li><li>Fault Code 195, (3-Wire Sensor) Coolant Level Sensor 1 Circuit - Voltage Above Normal or Shorted to High Source.</li><li>Fault Code 196, (3-Wire Sensor) Coolant Level Sensor 1 Circuit - Voltage Below Normal or Shorted to Low Source.</li><li>Fault Code 687, Turbocharger Number 1 Speed Low - Warning Level.</li><li>Fault Code 2551, Fuel System Overfueling.</li></ul><p>For Fault Code 153, Fault Code 195, and Fault Code 196, the pin numbers have been corrected to reflect the same pin numbers on the present wiring diagrams for ISX, Signature™, and ISX CM870.</p><p>For the Fault Code 687, the turbocharger speed sensor o-ring information was added to the &quot;Shop Talk&quot; section. The addition explains that in some cases the turbocharger original speed sensor o-ring can remain during sensor replacement. The new sensor is then installed with a new o-ring and creates excessive clearance from the sensor to the turbocharger shaft. This can cause fault code 687.</p><p>For Fault Code 2551, the direction in step 2A-1 of the troubleshooting procedure for fault code 2551 is misleading. The step has been changed to direct the correct course of action.</p>","tsb101998":"<h2>Revision to Main Bearings Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install step of Procedure 001-006. The text and a graphic have been revised.</p>","tsb101999":"<h2>Rocker Lever Cover, New Embedded Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is revising the Rocker Lever Cover, Procedure 003-011. The updates are including an additional remove and install procedure for the new rocker lever cover assembly, Part Number 3104387.</p><p>Engines built after September 7, 2006, will have a cover gasket embedded into the new rocker lever cover and will include the following items;</p><ul><li>Rocker lever cover</li><li>Cover gasket</li><li>Rocker lever cover isolators.</li></ul>","tsb102002":"<h2>Oil Pan Adapter Installation Update, Sealant Use Guideline</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Lubricating Oil Pan Adapter procedure to instruct when to use 3M spray and when to use sealant.</p>","tsb102004":"<h2>New Fault Codes 772 and 773</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces Fault Codes 772 and 773 for the QST30 engine.</p>","tsb102015":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Revision, Engine Brake Information</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Maintenance Schedule for Signature and ISX series engines to include engine brake replacement information.</p>","tsb102017":"<h2>Cylinder Head Inspection Specifications Update</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the following Clean and Inspect for Reuse specifications, for cylinder heads built after August 21, 2006 with the combustion face scallop, to Procedure 002-004:</p><ul><li>Valve recession</li><li>Operational recession</li><li>Valve recession variation between valves on same cylinder</li><li>Valve tip height</li><li>Insert bore depth.</li></ul>","tsb102020":"<h2>Revision to Symptom Tree, Lubricating Oil Pressure Low</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Symptom Tree <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666003\">3666003</a>-t105 for C and C8.3 Series engines. Unnecessary steps are removed and a reference bulletin is changed in &#x27;Correction&#x27; step 4.</p>","tsb102025":"<h2>Graphics Revision to Lubricating Oil Pressure Regulator (Main Rifle) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises and updates graphics in Lubricating Oil Pressure Regulator (Main Rifle) Procedure 007-029, for 6C, C8.3, ISC, and QSC8.3 engines.</p>","tsb102031":"<h2>New Fault Code, 143, Engine Oil Pressure Low-Warning</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the creation of a new fault code, 143, Engine Oil Pressure Low-Warning.</p>","tsb102032":"<h2>New Fault Code, 143, Engine Oil Pressure Low-Warning</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the creation of a new fault code, 143, Engine Oil Pressure Low-Warning.</p>","tsb102039":"<h2>Revision, Preparation Steps; Water Header Plate, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new procedure to remove and install the coolant header cover plate released with the 2007 cylinder block. The 2007 cylinder block features a new coolant return port that was specifically designed to provide a coolant return for the 2007 EGR cooler. The 2007 cylinder block is backwards compatible with older cylinder blocks, by virtue of installing a coolant header cover plate.</p>","tsb102042":"<h2>Revision to Install Step in Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises sealant, Part Number 3165150, in the Install Step in Cylinder Liner Procedure 001-028. The new sealant Part Number is 4918771.</p>","tsb102043":"<h2>Revision to Cylinder Head Procedure, Inspect Valve Spring Collet Seating</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Assemble step of Procedure 002-004, Cylinder Head, to add an inspection of the valve spring collet seating.</p>","tsb102053":"<h2>Spin-on Fuel Filter Procedure Update for Electronically Actuated Injectors</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 006-015, Fuel Filter, Spin-on, for QSK45 and QSK60 industrial and marine series engines with electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb102055":"<h2>Revised Fuel Lift Pump Procedure, Filtration System Update</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 005-045, Fuel Lift Pump, for QSK60 series engines with electronically actuated injectors, due to changes in the filtration system.</p>","tsb102071":"<h2>Revision, 12-VDC Specification Changes, Engine Brake Solenoid Valve Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the solenoid resistance specifications of each 12-VDC engine brake solenoid (wiring harness disconnected), as measured from the terminal to the body of the solenoid in procedure, Engine Brake Solenoid Valve, 020-012.</p>","tsb102076":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Fuel Pump Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 005-016 Fuel Pump for the QSK60 engine with electonically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb102077":"<h2>New Procedure, Fuel Pump Pressurizing Assembly</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new common Procedure 005-232, Fuel Pump Pressurizing Assembly, to be used in the QSK60 modular common rail system engines.</p>","tsb102079":"<h2>Revision, Step 5D, Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Step 5D of the Engine Performance Troubleshooting Tree for the ISX engines.</p>","tsb102083":"<h2>Revision to Install Step of Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the amount of turn when installing the lubricating oil filter, in Procedure 007-013, Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On).</p>","tsb102099":"<h2>Revision, Guided Step 2D-2, Fault Code 222</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Step 2D-2 in Fault Code 222 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Electronic Control System, Signature, ISX and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin 3666259. The air pressure sensor, <b>not</b> the air temperature sensor, should be replaced in the event of a pin-to-pin short circuit in this check.</p>","tsb102102":"<h2>Revision, Guided Steps 3C and 3D, Fault Code 2359</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Fault Code 2359 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, CM870 Electronic Control System, Signature and ISX Engines, Bulletin 4021334. The differential pressure tubes can now be checked for clogs without removing the tubes.</p>","tsb102103":"<h2>Revision, Shop Talk, Fault Code 2272 and All Guided Steps, Fault Code 2964</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the following in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, CM870 Electronic Control System Signature and ISX Engines, Bulletin 4021334:</p><ul><li>Fault Code 2272: The Shop Talk has been updated to warn that the fault may be caused by a broken EGR valve.</li><li>Fault Code 2964: All guided steps have been updated.</li></ul>","tsb102107":"<h2>Revisions, Remove Step, (Bearings, Connecting Rod) Procedure and Finishing Steps, (Gear Housing, Front) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p><ol><li>The connecting rod guide pin part number has been added to the Remove step of Procedure 001-005 (Bearings, Connecting Rod).</li><li>A reference to Procedure 019-042 (Engine Speed Sensor (ESS)) has been added to the Finishing Steps of Procedure 001-033 (Gear Housing, Front) for installing the crankshaft position sensor.</li></ol>","tsb102111":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Inspect for Reuse guidelines for Procedure 002-004.</p>","tsb102122":"<h2>Revision, Initial Check, (Air Leaks, Air Intake and Exhaust System) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is to update Procedure 010-024, Initial Check, (Air Leaks, Air Intake and Exhaust System). This update revises the Initial Check step to include disassembly and cleaning of the intake system as required.</p>","tsb102128":"<h2>Revision, Lubricating Oil Pressure Low Troubleshooting Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the entire troubleshooting symptom tree Lubricating Oil Pressure Low, t105.</p>","tsb102136":"<h2>QSK60 CM850 Modular Common Rail System Engine Introduction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic introduces the Cummins® QSK60 Engine with CM850 Modular Common Rail System. The QSK60 is a 16 cylinder engine with a 60 liter displacement. The engine has been designed to meet United States Tier 2 mobile off-highway emission levels. The United States Tier 2 mobile off-highway emission requirements became effective January 1, 2006 for ratings above 560 kW (751 hp).</p><p>The upgraded design includes a new high pressure modular common rail fuel system and advanced ECM. New electronically actuated injectors, pistons, turbocharger, and valve covers have also been incorporated into the configuration. The QSK60 MCRS will continue to utilize a 2-pump, 2-loop low temperature aftercooling system to deliver the intake manifold temperatures that are required for Tier 2 emission levels.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>General Engine Data</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QSK60 With CM850 Modular Common Rail System Engine Data</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Configuration</td><td>D593007CX03</td></tr><tr><td>Configuration</td><td>D593006CX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>V - 16</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>60 liter [3661 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>158.75 mm [6.25 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>190 mm [7.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>14.5:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration (Single Stage turbocharging)</td><td>Turbocharged and aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration (Two Stage turbocharging)</td><td>Turbocharged, intercooled, and aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate engine weight (Single Stage turbocharging)</td><td>7800 kg [17,196 lb] (estimate dry)</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate engine weight (Two Stage turbocharging)</td><td>9000 kg [19,842 lb] (estimate dry)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Engine ratings available for the QSK60 with CM850 Modular Common Rail System engine are essentially ratings from the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine. Tier 2 performance curves offer the same torque rise as Tier 1 curves. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Option Number</th><th>Rated Horsepower</th><th>Torque Peak</th><th>Altitude Capability (ft)</th><th>Turbocharger arrangement</th><th>Rating Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FR6502</td><td>1400hp @ 1800 rpm</td><td>4710 lb-ft @ 1300 rpm</td><td>10,000</td><td>Single Stage</td><td>Continuous</td></tr><tr><td>FR6490</td><td>1500 hp @ 1900 rpm</td><td>5042 lb-ft @ 1300 rpm</td><td>6,000</td><td>Single Stage</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR6452</td><td>2000 hp @ 1900 rpm</td><td>5805 lb-ft @ 1500 rpm</td><td>8,000</td><td>Two Stage</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR6574</td><td>2250 hp @ 1900 rpm</td><td>6299 lb-ft @ 1500 rpm</td><td>4,500</td><td>Two Stage</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR6545</td><td>2300 hp @ 1900 rpm</td><td>6512 lb-ft @ 1500 rpm</td><td>4,000</td><td>Two Stage</td><td>Restricted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine Dimensions</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dimension Description</td><td>Dimension</td></tr><tr><td>Overall height of Single Stage engine above the centerline of crankshaft</td><td>1176 mm [46.3 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall height of Two Stage engine above the centerline of crankshaft</td><td>1524 mm [60.0 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall height below the centerline of crankshaft</td><td>789 mm [31.1 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall length from rear face of flywheel housing to fan drive mounting surface</td><td>2608 mm [102.7 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Overall width at widest point</td><td>1588 mm [62.5 in]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Training for the QSK60 with CM850 Modular Common Rail System (MCRS), control system is contained in Cummins® Virtual College training modules. This will be a part of the High Horsepower Virtual College.</p><p>The cooling system is a 2-pump, 2-loop system that requires both an engine coolant loop radiator and a low temperature aftercooling (LTA) radiator.</p><p>The total system heat rejection has increased slightly as a result of the revised combustion characteristics required to meet Tier 2 EPA emission levels. Factors that contribute to this are increased turbocharger compressor outlet temperatures and increased air flow. Maximum top tank temperature, however, remains unchanged at 100°C [212°F]. The service interval of the corrosion filter is still 250 hours.</p><p>One of the key differences in the cooling system when compared to the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector is the water pump. The QSK60 MCRS engine is equipped with a water pump that incorporates the impeller for the engine coolant loop and the low temperature aftercooler coolant loop on the same drive shaft. The inlet for both circuits is on the right-bank side of the engine.</p><p>The torque converter cooler option remains the same and the corrosion filter continues to be required and remains unchanged. The service interval of the corrosion filter is 250 hours.</p><p>The cooling system is driven by a water pump that has two impellers driven off of a common shaft. This water pump is located in the same place as the water pump on the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine. Each impeller drives one of the cooling system loops. There are 2 inlets on this water pump, one for each circuit. See Figure 1 below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600819.png\" alt=\"08600819.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Water Pump</p><ol><li>Engine coolant impeller</li><li>Low temperature aftercooler coolant impeller</li><li>Engine coolant inlet (shown with optional inlet connection)</li><li>Low temperature aftercooler coolant inlet (shown with optional inlet connection)</li></ol><p>The low temperature aftercooler outlet connection and the engine coolant inlet and outlet connections are located in the same areas as the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector coolant connections. The connections have changed slightly. The low temperature aftercooler inlet connection has been moved to the water pump on the right bank of the engine. (See Figures 1 and 2). Please reference the installation drawing for more detailed information.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600816.png\" alt=\"08600816.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, Inlet and Outlet Connections</p><ol><li>Low temperature aftercooler bypass</li><li>High temperature engine coolant outlet</li><li>Low temperature aftercooler coolant outlet.</li></ol><p>A new option has been released to allow diversion of coolant to a torque converter. Selecting this option adds a coolant supply connection to the water pump housing. Corrosion filters will continue to be required and remain unchanged. The filters are available on either the pan rail or the front of the thermostat housing. Cab heater supply connections are available at the rear of the water manifold. Cab heater return connections are available at the inlet of the water pump.</p><p>The 2-pump, 2-loop cooling system employed on the QSK60 MCRS results in a cooling system that is slightly different from the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine. As mentioned previously, the low temperature aftercoolers are located on their own loop. The main engine loop now consists of the oil cooler, engine block, jacket water thermostats, and water pump. The two cooling circuits share a common top tank. See Figure 3 below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600817.png\" alt=\"08600817.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, Coolant Cooling Loop</p><p>The QSK60 MCRS uses an aftercooler similar to the aftercooler used on the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine. An aftercooler is a coolant-to-air heat exchanger used to reduce the temperature of the air entering the intake manifold. Unlike the QSK60 mechanically actuated injector engine, the coolant that is supplied to the QSK60 MCRS aftercooler core is on a separate loop from the engine coolant. This coolant loop <b>must</b> have its own radiator. The aftercooler radiator <b>must</b> be designed to provide coolant cold enough to cool the intake air to 60°C [142 °F] on a 25°C [77°F] ambient day. The two cooling circuits share a common top tank. See Figure 4 below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600818.png\" alt=\"08600818.png\"></figure><p>Figure 4, Aftercooler Coolant Loop</p>","tsb102142":"<h2>Revision, Fuel in the Lubricating Oil Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree T092, Fuel in the Lubricating Oil in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The correction for a cracked or porous cylinder head has been updated.</p>","tsb102149":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a correction to the torque requirements in the install step of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head).</p>","tsb102151":"<h2>Revision, Coolant Loss - Internal Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree T021, Coolant Loss - Internal in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The revision adds a step to check the air compressor air inlet and air outlet tubes for signs of coolant and moves the step for pressure testing the cooling system.</p>","tsb102157":"<h2>Revision, Summary Data, Overhead Set Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the summary data of Procedure 003-004, Overhead Set, in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The correct maximum and minimum brake running clearance is now specified.</p>","tsb102158":"<h2>Revision, Wobble Check, (Vibration Damper, Viscous) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Wobble Check step of Procedure 001-052, (Vibration Damper, Viscous), in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. A misspelling has been corrected.</p>","tsb102159":"<h2>Revision, Leak Test, Lubricating Oil Cooler Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Leak Test step of Procedure 007-003, Lubricating Oil Cooler, in the Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>. The leak test for the oil cooler assembly is most effective when performed in water below 7°C [44°F].</p>","tsb102172":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, (Bearing, Connecting Rod) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the connecting rod side clearance specifications to Procedure 001-005 (Bearing, Connecting Rod) in the Service Manual, Signature, ISX, and QSX15, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666239\">3666239</a>.</p>","tsb102183":"<h2>Revision, Loading Information, Engine Run-In (Engine Dynamometer) Procedure 014-006</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic advises the service channel of changes to the Engine Run-in (Engine Dynamometer) procedure for the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual. This change introduces a chart for determining the run-in load for QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p>","tsb102184":"<h2>Removal, Secondary Step of Guided Step 2, Fault Code 443</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose this Service/Parts Topic is to revise Fault code 443, Throttle Voltage Supply, by removing the supply voltage check in Guided Step 2.</p>","tsb102185":"<h2>New Procedure, Crankcase Breather (Internal)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to add a new procedure for the QSX15, Procedure 003-002, Crankcase Breather (Internal).</p>","tsb102215":"<h2>Revised Maintenance Schedule - Mechanically Actuated Fuel Injectors</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Section 9, Maintenance Procedures at 10,000 Hours, to include injector replacement at engine half life to rebuild.</p>","tsb102237":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Fuel Filter Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-017 (Fuel Filter Head) in Section 1. Changes include instructions for the removal and installation of filter spuds and a leak check in the Finishing Step.</p>","tsb102247":"<h2>Revision, Maintenance Schedule, Fuel Filter Change Interval</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic changes the Fuel Filter (Spin-On Type) change interval from 1,500 Hours, or 1 Year to 250 Hours, or 6 Months, in Maintenance Schedule, Procedure 100-002.</p>","tsb102248":"<h2>New Fault Code 595, Turbocharger Speed High (Calculated)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds new Fault Code 595, Turbocharger Speed High (Calculated).</p>","tsb102250":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Straight Thread Plug Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 017-011 (Straight Thread Plug) in Section 17. The torque specifications for metric straight thread o-rings plugs used on QSK45 and QSK60 engines have been included.</p>","tsb102253":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 001-026, Cylinder Block, to show the correct minimum value for the lower counterbore inside diameter (Lower Press Fit).</p>","tsb102254":"<h2>Revision, Test Step, Engine Run In (Engine Dynamometer) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 014-006, Engine Run In (Engine Dynamometer), to remove a reference to a service tool that is not available through QuickServe Online.</p>","tsb102258":"<h2>Revision, Specifications Section, Cooling System Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to update the Fan-on Intake Air Temperature value in the Cooling System section.</p>","tsb102270":"<h2>Addition, Fault Code 951, Bulletin 3666259</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of the Service/Parts Topic is to add Fault Code 951 to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Electronic Control System, Signature, ISX, and QSX15 Engines, Bulletin 3666259.</p>","tsb102273":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, (Crankshaft Seal, Front) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the part number for the crankshaft seal installer in the Install step of Procedure 001-023 (Crankshaft Seal, Front) in Section 1.</p>","tsb102275":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Flywheel Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 016-005, (Flywheel).</p><p>This update is to clarify the installation procedure for the ISX flywheel pilot bearing spacer.</p>","tsb102276":"<h2>Revision, Torque Value, Turbocharger Coolant Hoses Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque value for the turbocharger coolant return hose banjo fitting in Procedure 010-041, Turbocharger Coolant Hoses.</p>","tsb102279":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the specification for connecting rod and crankshaft side clearance when reusing the same connecting rod and crankshaft on the same journal of the crankshaft.</p>","tsb102282":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Fuel Inlet Restriction Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the measure step in Procedure 006-020 (Fuel Inlet Restriction) in Section 6 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>"};
